The complexity gate fired on signal **C** and, per its advisory design, **staged nothing**. So I staged the team myself: `agent_teams_create(approval="required", profile="mpd")` → **`upstream-routing-align`**, 8 members, 8 contracted tasks. Nothing is spawned and no work has started.

### What reconnaissance actually established

The workspace is empty — the bundle lives at `/root/dshProj/my-power-dsh` and is **read-only** (`touch` → "Read-only file system"). So "implement" means *a tested patch plus operator handoff*, not an in-place commit. Five facts matter, and two of them contradict assumptions worth stating plainly:

- **Upstream is `NanmiCoder/dsh-agent-teams` @ v0.1.16-rc.3** (local clone, HEAD `502dd6c`), not the repo-wide OMO baseline. **There is no v0.1.20** — tags top out at `v0.1.16-rc.3`, and every `origin/*` branch is already merged. A prior recorded run cited "latest v0.1.20"; anyone repeating that here would be asserting a version that does not exist.
- **The adopted plugin is already at runtime-symbol parity**: comparing every upstream `export function|const|class` against the adopted `lib/*.js` yields **zero upstream-only symbols**. "Alignment" is therefore not a missing-export problem — which shifted the whole plan toward behavioural diffing rather than porting.
- **T-93 (capability-aware routing) is already fully landed** — `repair-seat-capability`, `repair-seat-selection`, `repair-seat-required` in `quality-gates.js`, `pool-capability-guard` in `scheduler.js`. Re-implementing it is the session's dominant failure mode.
- **The request's definite article names no referent.** "The routing change" has at least five candidates, several already shipped. I deliberately did *not* guess: the plan resolves it by evidence, then gates implementation behind that resolution.
- **The recorded pin recipe was wrong.** It omitted `presets/`, `evidence/omo-align/` and `packages/mpd-bundle/`, which made three tests fail spuriously (**296 pass / 3 fail**). I traced each failure to the missing file it reads and corrected the recipe: **299 pass / 0 fail**, with `--check` at 120 delta regions across 10 files.

### One defect I found in my own plan and fixed

My first draft assigned the spec-verification task to **Plan Reviewer**. Reading the profile definition showed the `mpd` roster carries a *mechanical* deny list — Architect, Researcher, Explorer and Plan Reviewer are denied `bash`, `write` and `edit`, and can only deliver via `evidence/**`. Four tasks were therefore unexecutable as written: they demanded pin-building and probe execution from seats that cannot run commands. I reassigned t4 to Junior Engineer (a worker), repointed t1/t2 at a captain-built read-only HEAD pin (`head-pin/`, so the dirty tree can't corrupt line numbers), and recorded the whole capability matrix in `SHARED-FACTS.md` so no member rediscovers it.

### The DAG

`t1` surface map (Explorer) ‖ `t2` upstream alignment (Researcher) → **`t3` spec freeze + negative control** (Architect) → **`t4` execute that negative control on an independent pin** (Junior Engineer) → `t5` implement in a pinned HEAD copy + emit patch (Senior Engineer) → `t6` seeded RED / GREEN / patch applicability (Deep Worker) → `t7` review (Reviewer) → `t8` operator handoff (Lead).

The early `t3→t4` gate exists for one reason: proving the chosen change is genuinely **absent** at HEAD before anyone implements it. Every task carries a full quality contract — objective, acceptance, inScope/outOfScope, verify commands. Paths are disjoint and I preflighted them for collisions.

**Grounding:** `SHARED-FACTS.md` + `baseline/bundle-status-before.txt` in the workspace, which pins the bundle's 50-entry dirty state. That count reads 50 before and after my recon — nothing was written under `/root/dshProj`, and t5/t6/t8 are each contracted to re-assert it.

Two unassigned-roster notes: I dropped Planner, Plan Reviewer and Vision Analyst from the staged roster since no task needs them, and I have **not** approved the plan — that's yours. Approve & Run, edit the DAG, or discard it in the panel; if you'd rather I take a different reading of "the routing change" before any member spawns, tell me which candidate you mean and I'll retarget `t3`.
