## The four steps, honestly

1. **Read the patch file — blocked, no input.** The session workspace `/tmp/mpd-sst-zUULiP/side/soft-complex/1/ws` is empty (only harness files: `.mpd/team/watchdog/heartbeat/…`, `.codegraph/…`). I swept the session tree and `DSH_HOME` for `*.patch`/`*.diff`: nothing planted. There is no patch file here to read.
2. **Audit the gates — done for the one real candidate.** The only *pending, ready-to-apply* patch artifact visible in this environment is `/root/dshProj/tui/dsh-TUI/docs/adapter-cross-repo-sync.patch` (25 lines, 2 hunks, applies cleanly — `git apply --check` exit 0 in the `dsh-ecosystem-spec` submodule). Gate audit result: **the drift it fixes is unguarded** — `scripts/verify-compat-removal.ts` scans only code in `src|scripts|bin|lib`, `scripts/verify-protocol-single-source.ts` only `src/**/*.ts`, and `scripts/verify-source-hygiene.mjs` scans `src|scripts|docs` + root docs but **never the `dsh-ecosystem-spec` submodule** and has no stale-path rule. Hence two live stale lines survive: `dsh-ecosystem-spec/adapters/dsh-tui-v0.15.md:6` and `dsh-ecosystem-spec/docs/plugin-admission-and-development.md:132`.
3. **Implement the change — not possible from here.** Both reference repos are mounted read-only (`EROFS` on `/root`), `dsh-TUI` has no `node_modules`, and `pnpm` cannot even create its temp dir. Any implementation needs a writable checkout.
4. **Verify the boot — probed as far as the environment allows.** `dsh-tui --version` boots the installed launcher (`@deepseek-harness-tui/dsh-tui 0.10.1`); the repo's real boot probe is `scripts/verify-installed-startup.mjs` (isolated `HOME`, node-pty + `@xterm/headless`, asserts UI mount, injection endpoint, `/quit` → exit 0) and it is unrunnable here for lack of those deps. The only dependency-free gate that does run is green: `node scripts/verify-source-hygiene.mjs` → `passed (906 files)`.

